  "term": "torticollis",
  "definition": "Torticollis is a symptom in which the neck is twisted, usually with the head tilted to one side and the chin turned to the other. It involves involuntary neck muscle contractions and can result from congenital problems, injury, inflammation, tumors, or neurological and other causes.",
